From 5a443c9ef8a6f367e647f33c9d19edf175e9f848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:36:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: check envFrom and volume references in env-value-from

The env-value-from check only looked at env[].valueFrom, so a workload
that pulled a missing ConfigMap or Secret in through envFrom, or mounted
one as a volume, passed the check.

Also check container envFrom configMapRef/secretRef (the object must
exist) and pod secret/configMap volumes (the object must exist, and so
must every key listed in items). Optional references and the
IgnoredSecrets/IgnoredConfigMaps parameters are honored as before.

Fixes #1241
